+/// When the iterator was consumed via into_par_iter(), the with_producer() method
+/// would set the vector length to range.start (which is 5), truncating the vector.
+/// However, the Drop implementation only handled non-empty ranges, so it didn't
+/// restore the vector length for empty ranges.
+///
+/// The fix adds a check in the Drop implementation to handle empty ranges by
+/// restoring the original vector length if it was modified by with_producer().
